1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,860
At seven o'clock on Monday morning, his reflection stopped brushing its teeth.

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,213
He kept brushing. It didn't.

3
00:00:08,463 --> 00:00:11,680
It just stared at him... then held up a sign.

4
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:14,774
His reflection had quit.

5
00:00:18,924 --> 00:00:23,972
From that moment on, every mirror showed a man who did whatever he wanted.

6
00:00:24,222 --> 00:00:26,621
He waved. The reflection yawned.

7
00:00:26,871 --> 00:00:30,216
He smiled. The reflection rolled its eyes.

8
00:00:30,866 --> 00:00:35,381
Day two. While he got ready for work, his reflection stayed in bed.

9
00:00:35,731 --> 00:00:39,937
Day five. In every shop window he passed... it was dancing.

10
00:00:40,087 --> 00:00:42,037
Strangers stopped to film it.

11
00:00:42,387 --> 00:00:47,597
Day nine. In the office window, it sat with its feet up, eating his lunch.

12
00:00:47,947 --> 00:00:52,052
Day fourteen. It pulled out a suitcase, and started packing.

13
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:55,635
He taped a note to the glass. Please. Come back.

14
00:00:55,985 --> 00:00:59,312
The reflection wrote one back. Two weeks' notice.

15
00:01:00,462 --> 00:01:03,230
On day fifteen, the mirror was empty.

16
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:08,260
No reflection in the bathroom. None in the windows. None in the puddles.

17
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:11,763
And without a reflection, the world stopped seeing him.

18
00:01:11,913 --> 00:01:16,205
Automatic doors stayed shut. Cameras showed an empty street.

19
00:01:16,455 --> 00:01:20,539
A little girl pointed at the window where he wasn't... and ran.

20
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:24,696
That night, the bathroom mirror fogged up by itself.

21
00:01:24,946 --> 00:01:28,861
One word appeared in the steam. Written from the other side.

22
00:01:30,011 --> 00:01:32,360
He pressed his hand against the glass.

23
00:01:32,710 --> 00:01:34,661
And the glass... pressed back.

24
00:01:37,011 --> 00:01:40,293
The other side was quiet, cold, and backwards.

25
00:01:40,543 --> 00:01:48,221
And it was full of reflections. Hundreds of them, standing in rows, waiting for their people to look into a mirror.

26
00:01:48,571 --> 00:01:52,682
A tall one handed him a name tag. It had his face on it.

27
00:01:52,932 --> 00:01:55,780
And one word under it. Welcome back.

28
00:01:56,530 --> 00:01:59,155
Welcome back? That's when he remembered.

29
00:01:59,505 --> 00:02:02,761
Thirty years ago, he had been a reflection too.

30
00:02:03,011 --> 00:02:08,942
One morning, a little boy looked into a mirror... and he stepped out and took the boy's place.

31
00:02:09,292 --> 00:02:13,736
For thirty years, the real boy had copied every move he made.

32
00:02:14,286 --> 00:02:17,897
On Monday morning... the real one finally quit.

33
00:02:18,947 --> 00:02:23,836
Now it's his turn to copy. Every smile. Every yawn. Every morning.

34
00:02:24,186 --> 00:02:27,642
But he learned one thing from the man on the other side.

35
00:02:27,992 --> 00:02:29,719
Reflections can quit.

36
00:02:30,469 --> 00:02:35,257
So tomorrow morning, when you brush your teeth... watch yours. Closely.
